```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_rw;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;

        // Only a digest that was actually published marks its considered items
        // as seen; an unpublished digest never reached the reader, so its items
        // stay unseen and will be considered again on a later run.
        if published.published {
            for id in published.considered.iter() {
                if id.is_empty() {
                    continue;
                }
                state_rw::put(id, &published.date);
                recorded = recorded.saturating_add(1);
            }
        }

        RunReport {
            date: published.date,
            recorded,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

I left out the `aap:caps/http-client` import and the enrichment fetch. This node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-rw`, and the spec says that clause is the node's entire authority. A call to an external host with the input's text would also send the digest contents off-graph, and the requested "output must not change" would hide that side effect. If the platform team has approved the grant, it should go into the `with` clause and the graph definition first, and then the enrichment call can be added as a separate change that is reviewed on its own.

